WEBVTT


00:00:22.844 --> 00:00:25.904
<i>Hold on 'cause I'm letting go</i>


00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.516
<i>I'm gonna lasso your heart like a rodeo</i>


00:00:29.684 --> 00:00:33.347
<i>I'm gonna give you some
Till you want some more</i>


00:00:33.521 --> 00:00:37.252
<i>'Cause all I see is an open door</i>


00:00:37.425 --> 00:00:41.225
<i>And I see where it's leading me
All of this energy</i>


00:00:41.395 --> 00:00:44.990
<i>Been bottled up way too long
It's powerful, powerful</i>


00:00:45.166 --> 00:00:48.727
<i>You see what I'm getting at
I'm ready for all of that</i>


00:00:48.903 --> 00:00:52.430
<i>If I'm not a star, you're blind</i>


00:00:52.607 --> 00:00:55.974
<i>I've got rings on my fingers
And glitter in my hair</i>


00:00:56.144 --> 00:00:59.409
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:03.277
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:03.451 --> 00:01:07.478
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:07.655 --> 00:01:11.250
<i>I've got high heel stilettos
And I'm kicking in doors</i>


00:01:11.425 --> 00:01:14.553
<i>And kissing your ass
Ain't what my lipstick's for</i>


00:01:14.729 --> 00:01:18.495
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:18.666 --> 00:01:21.658
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:21.836 --> 00:01:25.328
Where's breakfast?
I want waffles, spaghetti!


00:01:25.506 --> 00:01:28.771
Spaghetti waffles! Whoo. Whoo!


00:01:28.943 --> 00:01:30.968
Victor. Victor.
Please wait in the house, please.


00:01:32.413 --> 00:01:35.246
My body is entering hunger shock.


00:01:36.617 --> 00:01:40.314
Oh, bad news.
The cat pooped in the den.


00:01:40.488 --> 00:01:43.787
Worse news, I used your blanket
to clean it up.


00:01:43.958 --> 00:01:45.892
- We don't have a cat.
- No kidding.


00:02:20.995 --> 00:02:24.556
Oh. L... Sorry.
I didn't think you'd be awake.


00:02:24.732 --> 00:02:25.892
You have an appointment...


00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:28.661
...with Guy Morgan,
I didn't think you'd wanna be late.


00:02:28.836 --> 00:02:31.771
Oh, look at you thinking. Cute.


00:02:31.939 --> 00:02:33.998
But I always have time for my portrait.


00:02:34.175 --> 00:02:35.699
Look alive. Paint.


00:02:36.143 --> 00:02:37.974
I'm feeling spiritually blocked.


00:02:38.145 --> 00:02:39.976
Draw me a sesame seed bath.


00:02:40.414 --> 00:02:41.540
Bath. Now.


00:02:42.516 --> 00:02:44.381
Now, make momma look more beautiful
and thinner.


00:02:45.753 --> 00:02:46.981
And make that water more quiet.


00:02:50.558 --> 00:02:52.651
- Bev, you awake?
- Of course I'm awake.


00:02:52.827 --> 00:02:55.421
If I waited for you, I'd never be on time.


00:02:55.596 --> 00:02:58.030
Lucky you never wait for me then.


00:03:11.512 --> 00:03:12.945
Victor, no.


00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.554
Uh, don't you want a glass?


00:03:21.722 --> 00:03:27.718
Hmm. Earthy. A tad fishy.
Lovely gravel finish.


00:03:28.195 --> 00:03:30.720
Did you let Victor put worms
in the blender again?


00:03:31.432 --> 00:03:33.127
Yes. I mean, no.


00:03:34.635 --> 00:03:36.227
I mean, it just happened.


00:03:36.771 --> 00:03:38.136
You know nothing can kill me.


00:03:39.307 --> 00:03:40.934
Nothing.


00:03:45.579 --> 00:03:48.446
Step on it, Katie.
I cannot be late for this meeting.


00:03:48.616 --> 00:03:49.981
Just run them over if you have to.


00:03:52.787 --> 00:03:55.813
Hello? No, the kids don't need a library.


00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:59.221
I am the dean, and the dean gets
what she wants, and I wanna remodel.


00:03:59.393 --> 00:04:02.851
You're just boring. I'm being honest.
I don't know what else to tell you.


00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:06.124
And I wanted my office done
for my meeting with Guy Morgan...


00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.961
...the music mogul, but no.


00:04:08.135 --> 00:04:10.330
And using Bollywood
as a theme for the dance?


00:04:10.504 --> 00:04:13.962
That's totally un-American.
I don't care if it was my idea.


00:04:15.643 --> 00:04:17.907
Hello.
Oh. Oh.


00:04:18.079 --> 00:04:20.775
I'm Dean Van Ravensway,
and you must be...


00:04:20.948 --> 00:04:24.042
- Guy Morgan.
- Ah, yes. Guy Morgan, a pleasure.


00:04:24.218 --> 00:04:25.708
You look like a man who knows things.


00:04:25.886 --> 00:04:28.446
Aha, even some things I shouldn't know.


00:04:28.622 --> 00:04:30.419
- And I'm Luke.
Great.


00:04:43.971 --> 00:04:47.930
<i>So tell me, Guy, is it true?
Are you the new judge on Idol?</i>


00:04:48.109 --> 00:04:51.476
Well, let's just say
that Randy may be in the doghouse.


00:04:51.645 --> 00:04:53.510
- Now, let's talk about my son.
- Of course.


00:04:53.681 --> 00:04:56.115
- Have you reviewed your schedule, Luke?
- Yes, I have.


00:04:56.283 --> 00:04:59.810
In fact, um, I'd like to add a music class.
Um, the music theory...


00:04:59.987 --> 00:05:03.548
Wellesley has a great business program.
That's why we're here.


00:05:04.058 --> 00:05:08.961
There are two types of people
in the music biz: Artists and businessmen.


00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:10.961
- Luke is a businessman.
- Of course.


00:05:11.465 --> 00:05:15.458
Katie, get in here. Look alive.
Make yourself useful.


00:05:18.939 --> 00:05:21.271
Luke is gonna need a tour of the campus.


00:05:21.742 --> 00:05:26.805
So text Bev and ask her
to escort Mr. Morgan around campus.


00:05:27.114 --> 00:05:30.242
Now, Luke, if you are half as talented
a producer as your father...


00:05:30.418 --> 00:05:33.478
The verdict's still out.
He hasn't earned it.


00:05:35.156 --> 00:05:37.420
Heard the story of how I started
in the music business?


00:05:37.591 --> 00:05:41.027
- Yes, everybody's heard it, Dad.
- Then everybody should know how it goes.


00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:45.524
There I was,
working for The Rolling Stones...


00:05:45.699 --> 00:05:47.530
...when Mick himself...
- Dad.


00:05:48.803 --> 00:05:52.000
Fine. As I said,
the verdict is still out on my son.


00:05:52.173 --> 00:05:55.939
He just produced an album
with the Fruity Dangers?


00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:57.771
Do you mean Danger Fruit?


00:05:58.946 --> 00:06:00.709
That record was amazing.


00:06:00.881 --> 00:06:03.850
I forgot what they were called because
they made me absolutely no money.


00:06:05.352 --> 00:06:07.820
Thank you. Rare I meet anyone
who's heard their album.


00:06:07.988 --> 00:06:10.889
What, are you kidding?
They're a cult phenomenon.


00:06:11.058 --> 00:06:12.719
I'm sorry. Why are you talking?


00:06:14.261 --> 00:06:19.824
What I need is for Luke to learn
to spot a commercially viable star.


00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.161
Image drives the bottom line, right?


00:06:22.336 --> 00:06:25.703
I feel you. Would we have Bieber Fever
if he were an ugly troll?


00:06:25.873 --> 00:06:28.034
Actually, he is a tad hobbit-like, isn't he?


00:06:28.209 --> 00:06:30.575
I'd like Luke
to produce your Semester Showcase...


00:06:30.744 --> 00:06:34.646
...to see if he can identify sellable talent.
- I produce the Semester Showcase.


00:06:35.783 --> 00:06:37.876
I will double your Showcase budget.


00:06:38.385 --> 00:06:40.751
I will invite every talent scout I know.


00:06:41.322 --> 00:06:43.449
This could be the beginning
of a relationship...


00:06:43.624 --> 00:06:45.592
...between Wellesley
and Kensington Records.


00:06:45.759 --> 00:06:47.750
Looks like we have a new producer.


00:06:47.928 --> 00:06:50.897
Oh, and this is my daughter, Bev.


00:06:51.332 --> 00:06:54.096
Bev, this is the platinum-selling,
Grammy-winning...


00:06:54.268 --> 00:06:57.169
...and very handsome producer,
Guy Morgan.


00:06:57.338 --> 00:06:59.169
Could you give his son, Luke, a tour?


00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:02.207
Sure. Would you like
to see the Wellesley perks?


00:07:02.376 --> 00:07:05.004
Um, yes, brilliant. Sure.


00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:07.470
- Katie.
I love your accent.


00:07:07.648 --> 00:07:09.240
Katie.
Wanna come over tonight?


00:07:09.416 --> 00:07:11.782
What are you still doing here? Go.


00:07:11.952 --> 00:07:15.353
Guy and I have things we need to discuss.
Out. Now.


00:07:15.956 --> 00:07:21.360
So, Guy, you've gotta tell me,
what was that like working under Mick?


00:07:30.237 --> 00:07:31.932
Watch out.


00:07:32.406 --> 00:07:34.431
- Dangerous balls.
- Ha, ha. Thanks.


00:07:35.442 --> 00:07:39.037
- So you womanned up and did it?
Hey!


00:07:39.213 --> 00:07:41.010
- Oh, I did it.
Hey!


00:07:41.181 --> 00:07:43.547
- What happened?
Can we have our ball?


00:07:43.717 --> 00:07:45.082
I didn't give my CD to Luke.


00:07:45.252 --> 00:07:48.244
I snuck it in his dad's bag.


00:07:48.422 --> 00:07:52.381
But Guy Morgan has your demo.
That's huge. What you need is a champion.


00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:54.289
No, what I need is to graduate.


00:07:55.129 --> 00:07:57.029
You giving our ball back or what?


00:07:57.197 --> 00:08:00.826
Oh, do you want this?


00:08:05.639 --> 00:08:08.904
She shoots, she scores.
Unlike you, soccer boy.


00:08:11.245 --> 00:08:14.976
Oh, so spill it. Is Luke Morgan
as hot as everyone Tweets he is?


00:08:15.149 --> 00:08:16.514
Hotter.


00:08:16.684 --> 00:08:18.311
You should ask him to the dance.


00:08:18.485 --> 00:08:20.715
Because I'm so forward with guys.


00:08:20.888 --> 00:08:23.448
First time for everything, right?


00:08:30.598 --> 00:08:32.293
- Hi, Luke.
- Hello.


00:08:32.466 --> 00:08:33.694
You have to hear my demo.


00:08:34.168 --> 00:08:37.228
It's a retro-funk-jazz explosion.


00:08:37.404 --> 00:08:39.599
Back off. I was here first.


00:08:39.773 --> 00:08:43.231
Hold on, hold up. Please hold on.
My boy does not want your demos yet.


00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:45.674
Walk away. Move along. Bye.


00:08:45.846 --> 00:08:49.213
It was nice chatting
or whatever that was.


00:08:49.483 --> 00:08:51.815
- Yes, hi, I'm, uh...
- Luke Morgan, right?


00:08:51.986 --> 00:08:53.510
Who is producing the Showcase.


00:08:53.687 --> 00:08:56.588
I don't think I'm gonna do the Showcase,
so I need to keep a low profile...


00:08:56.757 --> 00:09:00.193
Yeah, yeah. Listen close now.
There's two kinds of people in this school.


00:09:00.361 --> 00:09:03.888
There are the wannabes
and there's gonnabes.


00:09:04.064 --> 00:09:09.229
You and I, we're gonnabes. What do we do?
We stay away from the wannabes, all right?


00:09:09.403 --> 00:09:12.964
And girls named Yolanda. There are three
of them and they are certifiably...


00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:15.233
Crazy? You attract
crazy women? Shocking.


00:09:15.409 --> 00:09:18.310
It may seem like I don't have game,
but ladies love a listener.


00:09:18.479 --> 00:09:20.606
Plus, I'm telling you,
let me help you find acts.


00:09:20.781 --> 00:09:23.807
- Ah, so you're a talent scout?
- Well, bottom line, I'm a DJ.


00:09:23.984 --> 00:09:26.179
- Oh, you're a DJ as well?
- Check this.


00:09:34.728 --> 00:09:35.990
Whoa.


00:09:36.163 --> 00:09:39.257
Okay, yes. You could be very useful.
It was nice meeting you.


00:09:39.433 --> 00:09:42.095
You got a girl for the dance?
Because I can hook you up.


00:09:42.269 --> 00:09:43.429
Uh, no. Thanks.


00:09:43.604 --> 00:09:47.005
Uh, but what do you know
about Bev Van Ravensway?


00:09:47.174 --> 00:09:48.835
- Supposed to see her tonight.
- Bev?


00:09:49.009 --> 00:09:50.033
- Yeah.
- She's hot...


00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:52.678
...but the girl
is mad, mad drama, okay?


00:09:52.846 --> 00:09:55.246
I am talking to you
and you don't even know my name.


00:09:55.416 --> 00:09:57.316
- I'm Mickey O'Malley.
- Mickey O'Malley.


00:09:57.484 --> 00:09:59.111
A rarity in the Irish community.


00:09:59.687 --> 00:10:01.780
Om.


00:10:02.589 --> 00:10:05.217
RAVl: Om.
- Om.


00:10:05.392 --> 00:10:07.485
- Om.
- Om!


00:10:07.661 --> 00:10:10.186
This is not a contest, Ms. Gail.


00:10:10.564 --> 00:10:12.191
Just concentrate on your breathing.


00:10:13.701 --> 00:10:14.861
My butt is numb.


00:10:15.202 --> 00:10:18.399
If your butt is suffering,
then you are suffering.


00:10:18.572 --> 00:10:22.030
In fact, your entire life is suffering. Why?


00:10:22.209 --> 00:10:25.303
Because you crave
that which is meaningless.


00:10:25.479 --> 00:10:27.470
Are you calling me shallow?


00:10:28.549 --> 00:10:34.385
No, I'm saying to stop your craving
and release your butt.


00:10:34.555 --> 00:10:38.116
Just release it. Release it, yeah.
Release that butt.


00:10:38.992 --> 00:10:42.052
<i>Release that butt
Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:42.229 --> 00:10:44.823
<i>Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:44.998 --> 00:10:46.295
Mrs. Van Ravensway?


00:10:46.467 --> 00:10:48.992
What part
of "if you interrupt my meditation...


00:10:49.169 --> 00:10:52.366
...I will jerk your tail in a knot"
do you not understand?


00:10:52.539 --> 00:10:54.973
You told me
to tell you when dinner was ready.


00:10:55.142 --> 00:10:58.543
Oh, thank God.
I'm craving some bourbon.


00:11:02.316 --> 00:11:03.783
Victor.


00:11:03.951 --> 00:11:09.184
- Oh. Um, dinner's ready.
- Tell me something I don't know.


00:11:32.846 --> 00:11:37.283
Do you have any idea how stressful it is
to run this academy?


00:11:37.618 --> 00:11:40.109
Yes, I spent the money at the spa.


00:11:41.155 --> 00:11:43.817
<i>Five thousand dollars a night
is not very expensive...</i>


00:11:43.991 --> 00:11:48.553
<i>... when you think about the alternative,
which is me having a nervous breakdown.</i>


00:11:51.865 --> 00:11:52.889
<i>Ow.</i>


00:11:53.066 --> 00:11:55.500
<i>What are you doing?
I'm on the phone.</i>


00:11:55.669 --> 00:11:57.261
<i>- I'm cleansing.
Heh, heh.</i>


00:11:57.471 --> 00:11:59.701
Mac and cheese.


00:12:00.607 --> 00:12:03.735
<i>I don't need your spiritual counseling.</i>


00:12:04.278 --> 00:12:05.836
<i>I'm thinking of firing you.</i>


00:12:11.351 --> 00:12:14.718
Pace yourself, Ms. Gail,
or you will not be one with everything.


00:12:14.888 --> 00:12:18.221
Honey, that's what I got you for.
Now, make me one with everything.


00:12:19.626 --> 00:12:22.823
This Showcase is giving me the vapors.


00:12:22.996 --> 00:12:25.089
How did this become my life?


00:12:25.265 --> 00:12:28.257
Did I ever tell you all about the time
I nearly got my big break?


00:12:28.435 --> 00:12:29.925
Yes.
- Good.


00:12:30.103 --> 00:12:31.536
Then you all know how it goes.


00:12:31.972 --> 00:12:34.167
<i>I ain't gonna leap, I'm gonna jump</i>


00:12:34.341 --> 00:12:36.673
<i>Find my way right out of this dump</i>


00:12:39.513 --> 00:12:42.380
- I had talent, and they made me...
A laughingstock.


00:12:44.151 --> 00:12:45.448
Now look at me.


00:12:45.619 --> 00:12:48.110
I got two ungrateful kids...


00:12:48.288 --> 00:12:51.280
...a dwarfish, hairy, elfin servant...


00:12:51.458 --> 00:12:53.449
...and a random
tablecloth-wearing Asian...


00:12:53.627 --> 00:12:55.857
- Indian.
- Who makes no sense at all, ever.


00:12:56.029 --> 00:12:57.792
Why don't you have another drink, Mom.


00:12:59.333 --> 00:13:01.528
Katie, napkin me.


00:13:01.702 --> 00:13:04.193
I have got to impress Guy Morgan...


00:13:04.605 --> 00:13:07.836
...so I can stop pretending to care
about this insufferable school...


00:13:08.008 --> 00:13:11.774
...and we can all move to Hollywood where
no one pretends to care about anything.


00:13:11.945 --> 00:13:15.574
Mom, I think that you're forgetting
about the most important thing. Me.


00:13:16.516 --> 00:13:18.916
Guy will give me a deal
as soon as he hears me sing.


00:13:19.086 --> 00:13:21.680
- I doubt that.
- No, I've been practicing really hard.


00:13:21.855 --> 00:13:24.722
My voice teacher says
I've transcended to a whole new level.


00:13:24.892 --> 00:13:25.916
Yeah, I doubt it.


00:13:26.093 --> 00:13:28.653
When my first single drops,
I'll buy you that mansion...


00:13:28.829 --> 00:13:30.763
...in the Hollywood Hills...


00:13:30.931 --> 00:13:33.957
...and you can finally afford
to have your legs lengthened.


00:13:34.134 --> 00:13:36.159
- Oh, ba...
- Ms. Gail.


00:13:36.336 --> 00:13:38.304
- Miss Bev has clarity.
Katie.


00:13:38.472 --> 00:13:39.496
- You see...
- Look.


00:13:39.673 --> 00:13:43.541
- The lowly peasant tills the soil
for 40 years without any rain.


00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:47.111
But the unemployed salesman
who has recently discovered hydroponics...


00:13:47.281 --> 00:13:50.375
...all of a sudden gets disgusted by the...
- And see? No sense.


00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:52.848
- That didn't make any sense.
- Let me finish. You...


00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:54.954
Oh, I doubt it. You have me pray all day.


00:13:55.122 --> 00:13:57.352
- I don't feel nothing.
- You don't have a soul.


00:13:57.524 --> 00:14:00.721
No, you don't have soul.
- I have a many souls. I'll give you one.


00:14:00.894 --> 00:14:05.160
- Where's your third eye? Turn that thing on.
- I have a fourth eye too. You wanna see it?


00:14:05.332 --> 00:14:07.300
- What?
- Shh.


00:14:07.801 --> 00:14:11.328
I wanna be 6'4". Wow me, Bev.


00:14:13.874 --> 00:14:19.312
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:19.479 --> 00:14:22.039
Just stop. Stop the wowing, okay?


00:14:22.215 --> 00:14:24.308
What's wrong?
- Somehow you've gotten worse.


00:14:24.484 --> 00:14:26.213
I don't know how that was possible...


00:14:26.386 --> 00:14:29.014
...but there isn't enough Auto-Tune
that's gonna fix you.


00:14:29.189 --> 00:14:32.522
- Well, Katie's bad playing threw me off.
- I don't think it was that.


00:14:32.693 --> 00:14:34.320
Again.


00:14:34.494 --> 00:14:36.052
Really? Okay.


00:14:36.229 --> 00:14:41.861
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:42.035 --> 00:14:43.161
Ouch.


00:14:43.337 --> 00:14:46.397
I could belch the song better.


00:14:48.008 --> 00:14:50.169
Have you been drinking
the floor wax again?


00:14:50.344 --> 00:14:51.811
Anything to forget I live here.


00:14:51.979 --> 00:14:54.880
Ugh. My head is buzzing
like a skeeter on a septic tank.


00:14:55.048 --> 00:14:58.950
- Ravi, meditate me.
Good luck, buddy.


00:14:59.319 --> 00:15:02.982
Well, it doesn't matter,
because I have my own plan.


00:15:07.194 --> 00:15:09.560
Does it make me a bad person
that I kind of enjoyed that?


00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:11.459
No.


00:15:11.631 --> 00:15:13.929
Hmm. Nice work.


00:15:26.113 --> 00:15:29.412
- Guess who's on his way over.
- Not now, Victor, I'm busy.


00:15:29.583 --> 00:15:32.051
Guess or prepare to get creamed.


00:15:42.529 --> 00:15:45.623
Victor! Victor! Victor, stop!


00:15:50.504 --> 00:15:52.233
<i>I've got rings on my fingers</i>


00:15:52.406 --> 00:15:53.498
<i>And glitter in my hair</i>


00:15:53.673 --> 00:15:57.769
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:15:57.944 --> 00:15:59.275
<i>I'm gonna run...</i>


00:15:59.446 --> 00:16:02.210
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Victor, what are you doing?


00:16:02.649 --> 00:16:03.946
Victor!


00:16:04.117 --> 00:16:07.348
Victor, where did you put my clothes?


00:16:07.521 --> 00:16:09.682
- Surprise!
- What? No.


00:16:13.193 --> 00:16:14.820
I'm gonna kill you. Victor!


00:16:24.738 --> 00:16:25.898
Oh, hi, Katie.


00:16:26.073 --> 00:16:27.472
You are evil. Let me in.


00:16:27.641 --> 00:16:31.077
I control every lock on this property.


00:16:31.244 --> 00:16:32.905
Crap.


00:16:36.316 --> 00:16:38.011
This is insane.


00:16:38.185 --> 00:16:42.246
Yeah, try the shed, it's unlocked, idiot.


00:16:52.032 --> 00:16:54.125
You gotta be kidding me.


00:16:55.869 --> 00:16:57.496
Crap.


00:17:00.807 --> 00:17:04.402
How did such an untalented daughter
spring from my loins?


00:17:04.578 --> 00:17:08.378
Focus, Ms. Gail. We are making
an offering to your personal deity.


00:17:08.548 --> 00:17:10.675
Tell him to give me fame and fortune.


00:17:10.851 --> 00:17:12.546
Not exactly how it works.


00:17:12.719 --> 00:17:15.279
<i>Now, breathe through your Mula Bandha.</i>


00:17:15.455 --> 00:17:18.515
Oh, honey, if I could do that,
I'd get a million hits on YouTube.


00:17:18.692 --> 00:17:20.922
How much longer is this gonna take?
Ugh.


00:17:21.094 --> 00:17:23.221
The prayer or the fame and fortune?


00:17:25.565 --> 00:17:27.032
Ha, ha. See you later.


00:17:33.206 --> 00:17:35.071
Victor.


00:17:38.912 --> 00:17:40.345
Katie?


00:17:41.548 --> 00:17:43.778
- Luke.
- Katie.


00:17:43.984 --> 00:17:47.249
- Are you wearing a doormat?
- Yes.


00:17:47.420 --> 00:17:50.184
- Welcome.
- Why, thank you.


00:17:51.224 --> 00:17:53.055
The truth. Um...


00:17:54.361 --> 00:17:57.694
My stepbrother locked me
outside of the house.


00:17:57.864 --> 00:17:59.195
Naked.


00:18:00.233 --> 00:18:02.531
Oh, sorry. You should...
You should take my jacket.


00:18:02.702 --> 00:18:04.226
Oh.
- Oh, no, no.


00:18:06.673 --> 00:18:07.765
There.


00:18:07.941 --> 00:18:11.138
- Thanks. Now the pants.
- Hmm?


00:18:15.749 --> 00:18:17.376
I'm kidding.


00:18:17.918 --> 00:18:19.749
- You got me.
- Ha, ha.


00:18:20.086 --> 00:18:21.110
No, no.


00:18:21.288 --> 00:18:24.689
One more parent-teacher conference,
I swear I'm gonna lose it.


00:18:24.858 --> 00:18:27.053
Look at me. I'm an educator.


00:18:27.661 --> 00:18:32.325
I have no real skills. And I will die
before I go back to my daddy's farm.


00:18:32.832 --> 00:18:36.632
You tell my personal deity
to help me achieve Guy Morgan. Do it.


00:18:36.803 --> 00:18:39.397
I'll put another banana on the altar.


00:18:43.276 --> 00:18:44.937
What is that?


00:18:45.512 --> 00:18:47.776
Do you hear angels singing?


00:18:47.948 --> 00:18:49.916
Perhaps the gods
have answered your prayer.


00:18:51.117 --> 00:18:52.846
Hey. What...?


00:19:05.699 --> 00:19:08.190
<i>- This is Gail Van Ravensway.
Hello.</i>


00:19:08.368 --> 00:19:09.995
Guy Morgan here. How are you?


00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:12.297
Oh, well, hello, Guy.


00:19:12.472 --> 00:19:14.736
What a surprise
to see you calling this number.


00:19:14.908 --> 00:19:15.932
Do you hear this?


00:19:16.109 --> 00:19:17.770
<i>I can justify</i>


00:19:17.944 --> 00:19:19.639
That's the demo your girl, Katie...


00:19:19.813 --> 00:19:22.145
<i>... slipped into my briefcase.</i>


00:19:22.315 --> 00:19:24.510
And it sounds like money, dear.


00:19:24.684 --> 00:19:26.549
She gave you a CD?


00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:30.087
Oh, well. Well, ain't that the berries.


00:19:31.324 --> 00:19:35.192
Ravi, what frigging god did you pray to?


00:19:36.429 --> 00:19:40.525
Guy, yeah, it seems someone's
not being entirely honest here.


00:19:42.502 --> 00:19:44.697
Katie, somebody get that door!


00:19:45.839 --> 00:19:47.397
So...


00:19:48.275 --> 00:19:50.402
...that meeting today...


00:19:50.577 --> 00:19:53.375
...it was obvious
that your dad doesn't get you.


00:19:53.713 --> 00:19:55.772
He's an idiot for not liking your music.


00:19:55.949 --> 00:19:58.383
Well, it's... It's complicated.


00:19:58.652 --> 00:19:59.846
I'm gonna just, uh...


00:20:01.321 --> 00:20:03.221
Is it as complicated as me...


00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:06.518
...getting stuck outside
in only a welcome mat?


00:20:06.793 --> 00:20:10.524
That's not complicated.
That is a gift from God.


00:20:15.435 --> 00:20:18.233
Luke. Katie. What are you doing?


00:20:18.405 --> 00:20:21.465
Well, it seems your brother
is Satan's very own personal Mini-Me.


00:20:21.641 --> 00:20:23.905
Oh, I know, tell me about it. Come on in.


00:20:27.881 --> 00:20:29.542
Oh, my God, did you work out today?


00:20:31.217 --> 00:20:32.514
- Sit down.
- Ooh, look at this.


00:20:32.686 --> 00:20:35.780
- Ha, ha. Some lemonade.
- Why, thank you.


00:20:35.955 --> 00:20:38.423
You know, my stepsister,
she has body issues...


00:20:38.591 --> 00:20:40.752
...so I don't like
to discourage her nudity.


00:20:40.927 --> 00:20:42.121
That's interesting.


00:20:42.295 --> 00:20:45.059
- She's absolutely lovely...
- Would you like an appetizer?


00:20:45.231 --> 00:20:46.459
<i>Oh, fromage.</i>


00:20:46.633 --> 00:20:48.260
I only have cheese.


00:20:51.438 --> 00:20:53.406
I just got off the phone
with Guy Morgan.


00:20:53.573 --> 00:20:55.473
Your phone.


00:20:58.511 --> 00:21:01.378
He just loved that little demo
you left him.


00:21:01.548 --> 00:21:03.106
I have underestimated you.


00:21:03.683 --> 00:21:05.514
It'd make me proud
if I cared about you.


00:21:05.685 --> 00:21:08.779
- I didn't lie about anything.
- Oh, but, chicken, you did.


00:21:08.955 --> 00:21:11.583
At least that's what Guy thinks,
now that I've clarified.


00:21:11.758 --> 00:21:15.956
I told him it was Bev's demo
and that you stole it from her.


00:21:16.129 --> 00:21:19.394
- But you can't do that. That's my song.
- It's Bev's song.


00:21:19.566 --> 00:21:23.002
And Guy can't wait to see her perform it
at the Showcase.


00:21:23.169 --> 00:21:26.297
If you try to contact him, I'll deny
everything and lock you in the basement.


00:21:26.473 --> 00:21:31.604
- She can't sing to save her life.
- No, but you can, can't you?


00:21:32.879 --> 00:21:35.040
Now, let's hear this amazing voice.


00:21:40.453 --> 00:21:45.083
<i>Like a malignant tumor
She's got no sense of humor</i>


00:21:45.258 --> 00:21:49.354
<i>Just like a swollen blister
It's best to just resist her</i>


00:21:49.529 --> 00:21:53.295
<i>She's not exactly a witch
She's just a terrible bi...</i>


00:21:53.767 --> 00:21:55.428
Well, your lyrics stink.


00:21:55.602 --> 00:21:57.763
But Guy's right, you've got chops.


00:22:01.007 --> 00:22:03.703
Do you know what other instruments
I'm good at?


00:22:04.277 --> 00:22:07.735
I have a feeling I could get in trouble
with a question like that.


00:22:08.181 --> 00:22:10.149
I like trouble.


00:22:11.684 --> 00:22:12.810
Hey, kids.


00:22:14.120 --> 00:22:17.556
- Good evening, Miss Van Ravensway.
- Sorry, I need you to go. Now.


00:22:17.724 --> 00:22:20.488
Family emergency. I need Bev
to help me pass a kidney stone.


00:22:20.660 --> 00:22:24.494
- So she had a lovely evening. Ta-ta.
- Are you trying to ruin my life?


00:22:24.798 --> 00:22:30.031
I have figured out a way for you
to wow Guy Morgan in the Showcase.


00:22:30.236 --> 00:22:32.704
- So you do think I've improved?
- Oh, no, honey.


00:22:32.972 --> 00:22:35.532
But my month of spiritual devotion
has taught me...


00:22:35.708 --> 00:22:37.676
...that God works in annoying ways.


00:22:37.844 --> 00:22:40.904
How am I to wow Guy Morgan
if I supposedly can't sing?


00:22:41.080 --> 00:22:44.140
You can't, but Katie can.


00:22:44.317 --> 00:22:47.013
- What?
- I know. Like I said, annoying.


00:22:47.187 --> 00:22:50.486
We'll record her voice
and you will lip synch.


00:22:50.657 --> 00:22:52.488
What if I don't want to?


00:22:53.593 --> 00:22:57.324
Don't you get snarky with me,
you ungrateful toad.


00:22:57.497 --> 00:22:59.556
- I saved your life.
- You didn't do anything.


00:22:59.732 --> 00:23:01.996
- My dad married you.
- Yeah, and then he died.


00:23:02.168 --> 00:23:05.729
I tried to put you in foster care,
but they was all fulled up on ugly.


00:23:05.905 --> 00:23:07.395
- Funny.
- I thought it was...


00:23:07.574 --> 00:23:09.041
...because you don't wanna look bad.


00:23:10.643 --> 00:23:12.770
Katie, if you don't sing...


00:23:12.946 --> 00:23:16.074
...I'm gonna find a way for that savings
your dad left to disappear.


00:23:16.483 --> 00:23:20.681
That means, you forget college,
moving out, you're stuck here with me.


00:23:20.854 --> 00:23:24.688
But, pumpkin, we're gonna have
so much fun growing old together.


00:23:24.858 --> 00:23:27.759
Why don't you just have her perform
if you like her so much?


00:23:27.927 --> 00:23:30.191
Because, honey, look at you.


00:23:30.363 --> 00:23:32.490
You are a star.


00:23:32.665 --> 00:23:36.863
That is what Guy Morgan needs.
You, the star.


00:23:37.036 --> 00:23:38.594
I'm a star.


00:23:38.771 --> 00:23:42.935
- A bright, gassy star.
- Yes, you are.


00:23:43.109 --> 00:23:45.509
And Guy Morgan is gonna
give you a swimming pool...


00:23:45.678 --> 00:23:47.646
...shaped just like Colin Farrell.


00:23:47.814 --> 00:23:49.372
Every part of him.


00:23:49.549 --> 00:23:53.076
Or, Bev, you could just see every part
of Colin Farrell on the Internet.


00:23:53.253 --> 00:23:56.017
And just leave me out of this.


00:23:57.290 --> 00:23:59.850
- Okay, so how do we do this?
- First rule of Lie Club...


00:24:00.026 --> 00:24:01.926
...is don't talk about Lie Club.


00:24:02.529 --> 00:24:04.429
Which includes you, Katie.


00:24:04.597 --> 00:24:07.293
As far as everyone knows,
you can't sing.


00:24:07.467 --> 00:24:09.526
And no more talking to Luke or Guy.


00:24:09.702 --> 00:24:11.067
Are we clear?


00:24:11.504 --> 00:24:12.698
Crystal.


00:24:14.641 --> 00:24:17.633
Yeah, Dad, we're about to meet
some fresh talent right now.


00:24:17.810 --> 00:24:21.803
Remember when you signed Jay-Z?
No, you passed on him, my bad.


00:24:21.981 --> 00:24:24.449
Um, this is like that,
except it's gonna be brilliant.


00:24:24.617 --> 00:24:25.948
Yeah. Okay.


00:24:26.119 --> 00:24:28.246
- Yeah, okay. Bye.
- Dude, what'd he say?


00:24:28.421 --> 00:24:29.945
These guys you told me about are good?


00:24:30.123 --> 00:24:33.490
Yes. The Oral Majority has potential.
They'll be here any second.


00:24:33.660 --> 00:24:36.356
Talking about potential,
how was your little date with Bev?


00:24:36.529 --> 00:24:38.793
- Her mom kicked me out.
- I told you. Bev is drama.


00:24:38.965 --> 00:24:40.523
Technically, it was Gail's drama.


00:24:40.700 --> 00:24:42.827
But Bev's interesting, man. She's...


00:24:43.002 --> 00:24:44.469
I'm worried she's bonkers.


00:24:44.637 --> 00:24:47.470
See, my last girlfriend, she was hot,
but absolutely mental.


00:24:47.640 --> 00:24:50.302
I need a girl who's not gonna be
shipped to the loony bin.


00:24:50.476 --> 00:24:52.239
Hang on, I'm gonna hit the facilities.


00:24:52.412 --> 00:24:54.107
Facilities. That's a new one.


00:24:54.547 --> 00:24:57.243
- Hey, man. Sorry we're late.
- Hey, what's good, y'all?


00:24:57.417 --> 00:25:00.147
Nobody talks to my boy
until he comes from the facilities.


00:25:00.320 --> 00:25:01.514
We're here to impress.


00:25:01.688 --> 00:25:03.952
- Clear, right?
- Got it.


00:25:07.794 --> 00:25:10.262
<i>When you're fighting just to keep it sane</i>


00:25:10.430 --> 00:25:12.694
<i>Throw your will
At the eye of the hurricane</i>


00:25:12.865 --> 00:25:15.060
<i>- Sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:15.234 --> 00:25:18.601
<i>- Help me sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:18.771 --> 00:25:21.296
<i>If you wanna find out who you are
Stop running</i>


00:25:21.474 --> 00:25:24.739
<i>In the end you'll figure out
It's all about nothing</i>


00:25:24.911 --> 00:25:30.213
<i>All night, it's gonna be all right
Hey, hey, hey, hey</i>


00:25:30.383 --> 00:25:37.118
<i>All right
Turn your dreams into your life</i>


00:25:38.324 --> 00:25:39.814
That's good.


00:25:46.866 --> 00:25:50.165
I'm clean. No one followed me.
And I got your intel.


00:25:51.004 --> 00:25:53.336
Oh, Katie, baby, your life sucks.


00:25:53.506 --> 00:25:55.406
Trust me, it gets worse.


00:25:56.442 --> 00:26:00.037
Okay, dude, those guys, they
just went Oral Majority on me in there...


00:26:00.213 --> 00:26:02.408
- I was trying to hold them back...
- You're right.


00:26:02.582 --> 00:26:04.516
They have potential and they're great.


00:26:04.684 --> 00:26:09.917
But first, my talent-finding friend,
promise me no more auditions in the bogs.


00:26:10.089 --> 00:26:12.284
- The what?
- The loo.


00:26:12.825 --> 00:26:14.588
- Bathroom. Toilet.
- Got it.


00:26:14.761 --> 00:26:17.355
All right. Okay, come on.
I wanna show you something.


00:26:17.964 --> 00:26:21.263
So now I have to rehearse in secret.


00:26:21.434 --> 00:26:22.901
Why not not rehearse?


00:26:23.069 --> 00:26:25.094
Make Bev sound bad. What do you care?


00:26:25.271 --> 00:26:28.263
No song, no savings account. No life.


00:26:30.443 --> 00:26:32.877
People. Coming. Now.


00:26:36.416 --> 00:26:38.247
Okay.


00:26:38.818 --> 00:26:41.184
Dude, what are we doing?
The suspense is killing me.


00:26:41.521 --> 00:26:43.284
Can you grab the mike?


00:26:43.456 --> 00:26:45.447
Not about to serenade
a brother, are you?


00:26:45.625 --> 00:26:47.456
Dude, with bromance, comes a fine line.


00:26:47.627 --> 00:26:49.925
That I shall not cross.


00:26:50.396 --> 00:26:52.694
So sing something.


00:26:54.367 --> 00:26:55.834
Okay.


00:26:59.972 --> 00:27:02.770
<i>I'm lost in a world
That rattles my brain</i>


00:27:02.942 --> 00:27:05.433
<i>I'm cleaning up my life
From the mess you made</i>


00:27:05.611 --> 00:27:07.010
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:07.480 --> 00:27:09.471
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:11.284 --> 00:27:13.752
<i>My soul's in debt, but my bills are paid</i>


00:27:13.920 --> 00:27:16.445
<i>I'd give anything just to make an escape</i>


00:27:16.622 --> 00:27:18.214
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:18.725 --> 00:27:20.352
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:21.360 --> 00:27:24.295
<i>So you can keep
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:24.464 --> 00:27:26.796
<i>Baby, you're rockin'
But there ain't no way I'm ever letting you in</i>


00:27:26.966 --> 00:27:28.433
<i>He's amazing.</i>


00:27:29.836 --> 00:27:31.497
<i>Not again</i>


00:27:32.438 --> 00:27:35.271
<i>So keep on
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:35.441 --> 00:27:40.640
<i>But, baby, you're better off walking
'Cause I ain't gonna let you in</i>


00:27:40.813 --> 00:27:42.371
<i>Never again</i>


00:27:43.483 --> 00:27:46.077
<i>I went out on a limb again</i>


00:27:46.252 --> 00:27:48.812
<i>I guess I had to lose to win</i>


00:27:48.988 --> 00:27:53.357
<i>I was too confused to know
Which way to turn</i>


00:27:54.761 --> 00:27:57.423
<i>- And she could be a millionaire...
- Crap.</i>


00:27:57.597 --> 00:27:59.861
<i>- Gail needs me to drive her home.
- I don't care</i>


00:28:00.032 --> 00:28:02.694
<i>'Cause, baby, there's nobody home</i>


00:28:02.869 --> 00:28:05.360
<i>Nobody's home at all, yeah</i>


00:28:09.842 --> 00:28:11.969
- What? Did you write that?
- Yeah.


00:28:12.145 --> 00:28:14.773
Reminds me of, um... Uh...


00:28:14.947 --> 00:28:18.280
- Danger Fruit, right? Danger Fruit.
- Ha, ha. Because I wrote their album too.


00:28:18.551 --> 00:28:21.042
Shut up. Took me forever
to find that bootleg online.


00:28:21.220 --> 00:28:23.211
- I love that album. That's crazy.
- Yeah.


00:28:23.389 --> 00:28:25.687
My dad doesn't know.
And he thought the record...


00:28:25.858 --> 00:28:27.553
...was a pile of crap.


00:28:27.827 --> 00:28:29.522
He thinks writing's a waste of time.


00:28:29.962 --> 00:28:33.796
Because he basically wants me
to be like him. Only with better hair.


00:28:34.267 --> 00:28:38.363
But the first thing I thought when
I heard those guys in the urinals was...


00:28:38.538 --> 00:28:39.562
...good acoustics.


00:28:39.972 --> 00:28:43.806
Second thought was these guys,
these guys could be great.


00:28:43.976 --> 00:28:45.568
If you gave them your song.


00:28:46.979 --> 00:28:48.640
Mate, that's a brilliant idea.


00:28:49.382 --> 00:28:52.078
- So put them in the Showcase?
- Put them in the Showcase.


00:28:52.251 --> 00:28:53.582
Yeah.


00:28:55.254 --> 00:29:01.784
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:29:02.094 --> 00:29:03.391
You wrote that song today?


00:29:03.563 --> 00:29:07.021
- You've been home for what, two hours?
- It's like an answer to his song.


00:29:07.300 --> 00:29:08.597
You really like this guy.


00:29:08.768 --> 00:29:10.463
Yeah, I'm an idiot.


00:29:10.636 --> 00:29:12.831
You have to sing that for him.


00:29:13.005 --> 00:29:16.497
What if you sang to him in secret?


00:29:18.311 --> 00:29:21.109
At the dance. Ta-da.


00:29:24.717 --> 00:29:27.550
Okay, I know the card's
like, really cheesy, but...


00:29:29.589 --> 00:29:32.057
Oh, God, I hope you like it.


00:29:32.391 --> 00:29:35.883
Ange, it's beautiful,
but are you crazy?


00:29:36.062 --> 00:29:38.087
No, I know you're crazy.


00:29:38.264 --> 00:29:39.288
Am not.


00:29:40.333 --> 00:29:43.325
- What if he doesn't even like me?
- You'll both be in disguise.


00:29:43.502 --> 00:29:46.198
It's your chance to see
if he was really flirting with you.


00:29:46.372 --> 00:29:48.932
I was naked. Of course he was flirting.


00:29:49.108 --> 00:29:51.804
And why even torture myself?
It's not like I can have him.


00:29:51.978 --> 00:29:53.912
Why not? Tell him how you feel.


00:29:54.080 --> 00:29:58.107
If he feels the same way, you can reveal
your hot self and he won't tell Gail.


00:29:58.484 --> 00:30:01.578
And if he hates the song,
leave the disguise on.


00:30:04.523 --> 00:30:06.047
Okay.


00:30:06.359 --> 00:30:07.951
I'm going to the dance.


00:30:08.127 --> 00:30:09.458
That's my girl.


00:30:09.729 --> 00:30:13.722
<i>Maurice, no, no.
Again, in Français, longer legs.</i>


00:30:13.900 --> 00:30:17.199
I wouldn't go in your closet
for a little while if I were you.


00:30:17.370 --> 00:30:19.133
What? Why?


00:30:19.305 --> 00:30:20.670
Hey. Wake up.


00:30:24.577 --> 00:30:26.135
Katie!


00:30:26.312 --> 00:30:29.748
The cat has pooped in my closet.
I need you to clean it up.


00:30:29.916 --> 00:30:31.406
Go.


00:30:31.584 --> 00:30:33.313
I told you we don't have a cat.


00:30:33.486 --> 00:30:34.817
Angie, heads up.


00:30:36.789 --> 00:30:38.086
Katie!


00:30:43.296 --> 00:30:45.025
What's going on?


00:30:45.197 --> 00:30:46.630
Nothing.


00:30:46.799 --> 00:30:49.927
I am, uh, re-organizing and labeling. I...


00:30:50.102 --> 00:30:52.400
I took up crochet.
Do you want new socks?


00:30:52.571 --> 00:30:56.632
I would make you a sweater, but I hear
that the arms, that they're really hard.


00:30:59.879 --> 00:31:04.043
Oh, you thought you could sneak off
and go to the dance.


00:31:04.216 --> 00:31:06.446
After what you pulled today with Guy.


00:31:06.619 --> 00:31:08.052
Oh, no, no.


00:31:08.220 --> 00:31:10.711
Oh, no, no, no.


00:31:10.890 --> 00:31:13.188
You're on Victor watch tonight...


00:31:13.359 --> 00:31:16.055
...tomorrow night and every night.


00:31:16.228 --> 00:31:17.252
Fun.


00:31:17.430 --> 00:31:20.558
I'll give Victor all the mothering
you don't have time for.


00:31:20.733 --> 00:31:24.134
Oh, I wish you could be my mommy.


00:31:25.004 --> 00:31:27.029
I'm off to my cinnamon colonic.


00:31:31.010 --> 00:31:33.376
Hey. Get down.
You're gonna break yourself.


00:31:33.713 --> 00:31:35.977
Or worse, the furniture.


00:31:36.282 --> 00:31:39.376
Hello?
- Hey.


00:31:39.652 --> 00:31:42.815
- You look like you're having fun.
- Always.


00:31:43.155 --> 00:31:46.215
Well, I couldn't let you not go to the dance
without me.


00:31:46.392 --> 00:31:48.792
Besides, we have six hours
of shirtless Team Jacob.


00:31:48.961 --> 00:31:51.896
So let's just get this party started.


00:31:52.064 --> 00:31:56.091
- So is Victor driving you nuts?
- I swear to you, he's not human.


00:31:56.369 --> 00:31:59.668
I mean, can you really blame him, though?
Just look at this family.


00:32:00.873 --> 00:32:02.170
Victor, what are you doing?


00:32:12.151 --> 00:32:14.415
Oh, no. Great.


00:32:14.587 --> 00:32:16.782
Eh, she actually looks prettier
that way.


00:32:17.390 --> 00:32:20.416
True. Ugh. Whatever.


00:32:21.594 --> 00:32:24.722
Why did I ever think that tonight
could've been something special.


00:32:25.498 --> 00:32:27.762
Think Bev's all over Luke at the dance
right now?


00:32:27.933 --> 00:32:30.231
They're probably making out. See?


00:32:30.403 --> 00:32:33.600
- Victor, give it a rest.
- Just check it out. Come on.


00:32:36.809 --> 00:32:39.437
<i>Luke is gonna produce
whoever wins the Showcase.</i>


00:32:39.612 --> 00:32:42.672
<i>So we need a little insurance.</i>


00:32:42.848 --> 00:32:46.045
<i>- I know what I'm doing, Mother.
Do you?</i>


00:32:46.952 --> 00:32:49.819
I can't take it anymore, okay?


00:32:49.989 --> 00:32:52.048
I'm taking my life into my own hands.


00:32:52.224 --> 00:32:53.316
I'm talking to Luke.


00:32:53.926 --> 00:32:56.417
- Finally.
- Okay, but we have gotta be home...


00:32:56.595 --> 00:32:58.062
...before Gail gets here.


00:32:58.798 --> 00:33:00.129
What about the demon spawn?


00:33:00.299 --> 00:33:01.323
Mm-hm.


00:33:01.500 --> 00:33:02.899
Right.


00:33:03.903 --> 00:33:05.302
Okay, just watch him.


00:33:08.374 --> 00:33:09.636
Hmm.


00:33:14.447 --> 00:33:16.438
Is that all you've got, Angela?


00:33:17.116 --> 00:33:18.140
Ravi?


00:33:19.819 --> 00:33:22.344
My sister could catch that, jerknut.


00:33:22.521 --> 00:33:24.955
Put some nuts in that sack, ref.


00:33:27.093 --> 00:33:29.653
Miss Katie, I am most startled.


00:33:29.829 --> 00:33:31.023
Obviously.


00:33:31.564 --> 00:33:34.055
All right. All right. Don't hate me.


00:33:34.233 --> 00:33:35.791
Okay, don't hate me. I'm sorry.


00:33:35.968 --> 00:33:39.335
But my name ain't Ravi. It's Tony.


00:33:39.872 --> 00:33:43.000
- Tony.
- Tony Gupta from Jersey.


00:33:43.175 --> 00:33:45.837
- From Jersey.
- I am half Indian.


00:33:46.212 --> 00:33:49.613
My friends call me Meatball
because I'm half Italian.


00:33:49.782 --> 00:33:51.647
Truth is I always wanted to be an actor.


00:33:52.017 --> 00:33:53.541
But I never got my shot.


00:33:53.719 --> 00:33:55.949
I'm working at KFC,
and one day, Gail comes in...


00:33:56.122 --> 00:33:58.522
...she's like, "Are you Indian?"
I'm like, "What?"


00:33:58.691 --> 00:34:00.886
She's like, "Are you a guru?"
I'm like:


00:34:01.060 --> 00:34:02.550
"Who is asking?"


00:34:02.828 --> 00:34:06.195
She says, "Someone
who's paying for some spiritual guidance."


00:34:06.365 --> 00:34:08.959
And I'm like, "Whaa! It's a miracle!"


00:34:09.135 --> 00:34:13.504
I finally get a chance to do
a total immersion into a character.


00:34:13.806 --> 00:34:16.070
Real training and I get paid.
Are you kidding me?


00:34:16.242 --> 00:34:18.642
Ravi is my King Lear.


00:34:18.978 --> 00:34:21.606
<i>You wanna hear
the monologue from My Fair Lady?</i>


00:34:21.780 --> 00:34:22.974
- Oy, mate.
- No, thanks.


00:34:24.183 --> 00:34:26.879
I'm sorry I barged in. Whoops.


00:34:29.688 --> 00:34:33.351
Your secret's safe with me, okay?
But I need to ask you a favor.


00:34:34.026 --> 00:34:36.085
- Meatball.
- Ha, Meatball.


00:34:36.262 --> 00:34:38.730
Please watch Victor tonight
so I can go to the dance?


00:34:38.898 --> 00:34:39.956
Are you kidding me? Done.


00:34:41.534 --> 00:34:42.865
Blow it up.


00:34:44.803 --> 00:34:46.361
Thank you.


00:34:56.182 --> 00:34:57.581
Whoa.


00:34:57.750 --> 00:35:00.378
How am I supposed to find Luke
if everybody's got a mask?


00:35:00.553 --> 00:35:03.613
I never said this was
gonna be easy. Let's do some recon.


00:35:04.990 --> 00:35:07.322
I am Assistant Principal
Dorothy Plumberg.


00:35:07.493 --> 00:35:10.724
No drinking. No texting. No kissing.


00:35:13.432 --> 00:35:16.401
Luke? No. Luke Morgan?


00:35:16.569 --> 00:35:20.198
No leaving the premises
and no experiencing joy of any kind.


00:35:20.906 --> 00:35:23.238
Luke? Ugh.


00:35:28.614 --> 00:35:30.047
Where is he?


00:35:30.883 --> 00:35:33.681
That reminds me.
I got a new act for you to listen to.


00:35:33.852 --> 00:35:35.513
- Now?
- No time like it.


00:35:35.688 --> 00:35:38.122
- Dude, not again...
- We're called Big Pain Ticket.


00:35:41.627 --> 00:35:45.188
<i>I wanna kiss your apocalypse</i>


00:35:45.364 --> 00:35:48.697
<i>Wrap you in my Armageddon</i>


00:35:48.867 --> 00:35:51.062
<i>Sing you a twisted serenade</i>


00:35:51.270 --> 00:35:54.000
They're good, but I'm worried
that chain saw's unsafe.


00:35:54.173 --> 00:35:56.607
Dude, the chain saw's,
like, the best part.


00:36:03.415 --> 00:36:04.473
I think I found him.


00:36:04.650 --> 00:36:06.914
Well, he is blond.


00:36:10.022 --> 00:36:12.320
Oh, my God, what is she doing here?


00:36:14.226 --> 00:36:16.524
I hate teenage desperation.


00:36:16.695 --> 00:36:18.094
What are you doing here?


00:36:18.264 --> 00:36:21.097
Oh, honey, the prize pig
doesn't win the blue ribbon...


00:36:21.267 --> 00:36:23.292
...by covering up its third best asset.


00:36:23.469 --> 00:36:26.404
A, what does that even mean
and, B, did you just call me a pig?


00:36:26.572 --> 00:36:28.403
Honey, I saw you making sweet love...


00:36:28.574 --> 00:36:31.042
...to a plate of Swedish meatballs
at the snack table.


00:36:33.479 --> 00:36:35.606
It's now or never, babe.


00:36:37.149 --> 00:36:40.585
- What if she recognizes me?
- I'll distract her. Go.


00:36:40.753 --> 00:36:42.948
- So was I right or was I right?
- You were right.


00:36:43.122 --> 00:36:45.989
You have very cool taste.
Any more auditions in the men's...


00:36:46.158 --> 00:36:48.092
...and you're fired.


00:36:51.130 --> 00:36:54.657
- I know your secret.
- Which secret is that?


00:36:57.269 --> 00:36:58.759
I heard you sing at school.


00:36:59.004 --> 00:37:00.130
You were amazing.


00:37:00.306 --> 00:37:01.364
Do I know you?


00:37:05.711 --> 00:37:08.305
- I wanna show you something.
- What's your name?


00:37:10.649 --> 00:37:12.708
Angela, what are you doing?


00:37:13.352 --> 00:37:15.843
I'd like to make a request.


00:37:20.359 --> 00:37:23.192
I will make your night. I promise.


00:37:23.362 --> 00:37:24.727
Miss Van R.


00:37:25.364 --> 00:37:27.764
Is it true you wanted to be a dancer
when you were younger...


00:37:27.933 --> 00:37:29.127
...but were never good enough?


00:37:30.502 --> 00:37:32.163
Who told you that?


00:37:49.888 --> 00:37:51.321
Well, now, how lovely.


00:37:51.490 --> 00:37:54.687
But I've seen better dancing
in a Filipino prison, sugar.


00:37:54.860 --> 00:37:55.986
Oh!


00:37:56.161 --> 00:38:00.393
Really? Because I think
I just challenged you to a dance battle.


00:38:04.737 --> 00:38:07.831
Would Luke Morgan please pick up
the white courtesy phone?


00:38:08.006 --> 00:38:10.907
Luke Morgan, white courtesy phone.


00:38:15.681 --> 00:38:18.411
Hold on. What is that?
You've never seen a guitar before?


00:38:18.751 --> 00:38:21.447
You hid a guitar in there.
You hiding anything else?


00:38:21.620 --> 00:38:22.882
Follow me.


00:38:27.926 --> 00:38:29.757
Oh, wow.


00:38:32.231 --> 00:38:37.794
Madam, while your exquisite eyes
tell of a radiant, but mischievous beauty...


00:38:38.670 --> 00:38:40.570
...I have grown impatient.


00:38:40.739 --> 00:38:44.436
Off with your veil,
so that I may know the truth.


00:38:45.944 --> 00:38:47.138
Or not.


00:38:49.415 --> 00:38:52.441
I'm hoping this answers
a lot of your questions.


00:38:58.657 --> 00:39:02.218
<i>I can see it from the spark in your eyes</i>


00:39:03.529 --> 00:39:07.761
<i>You believe in all the things
You've denied</i>


00:39:07.933 --> 00:39:11.460
<i>You wanna fly
And leave your worries behind</i>


00:39:11.637 --> 00:39:15.630
<i>Don't you? Don't you?</i>


00:39:17.609 --> 00:39:20.942
<i>Well, now I'm knocking
At your front door</i>


00:39:22.714 --> 00:39:26.411
<i>And I'm looking for the right cure</i>


00:39:27.085 --> 00:39:30.782
<i>I'm still a little bit unsure</i>


00:39:31.256 --> 00:39:34.089
Okay, now take off that veil.


00:39:34.560 --> 00:39:35.652
Uh-uh.


00:42:14.586 --> 00:42:17.180
I think I've blown something.


00:42:17.356 --> 00:42:20.416
Does anyone else smell cinnamon?


00:42:23.028 --> 00:42:24.586
Move it, fatso.


00:42:26.331 --> 00:42:32.930
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:42:33.672 --> 00:42:37.301
Okay, you are blowing my mind.
You have to show me who you are.


00:42:49.855 --> 00:42:51.288
- We have to go.
- What?


00:42:51.456 --> 00:42:53.481
- Come.
- No, Ange.


00:42:53.659 --> 00:42:56.219
In the middle of a really big moment
right now.


00:42:56.395 --> 00:42:58.363
Someone had an accident
and went home.


00:43:00.832 --> 00:43:02.197
I'm so sorry.


00:43:02.901 --> 00:43:04.129
What...? You...?


00:43:04.836 --> 00:43:06.497
Hey. Wait.


00:43:06.672 --> 00:43:07.900
But who are you?


00:43:08.073 --> 00:43:10.667
Over here. Go, go, go.


00:43:18.817 --> 00:43:21.843
- We beat her.
- I love you for this.


00:43:40.305 --> 00:43:42.330
Interesting babysitting attire.


00:43:43.108 --> 00:43:46.043
I should've known
you'd go behind my back again.


00:43:46.478 --> 00:43:49.413
And that Paula Abdul wannabe,
trying to distract me.


00:43:49.748 --> 00:43:51.943
Don't talk about her like that.


00:43:53.952 --> 00:43:57.115
Your friend wants to be a choreographer,
if memory serves.


00:43:57.289 --> 00:44:00.850
She might've made a decent one
if she hadn't gotten herself expelled.


00:44:01.026 --> 00:44:03.290
Guess she can kiss
them Juilliard dreams goodbye.


00:44:03.462 --> 00:44:06.522
Look, I'll do whatever you want.
Okay? Just leave Ange out of this.


00:44:06.832 --> 00:44:09.960
That depends if you pull another stunt
like tonight, sugar.


00:44:10.869 --> 00:44:13.997
- I won't.
- I'll be taking this.


00:44:20.512 --> 00:44:23.743
Only her eyes were piercing out
through this veil, but her voice...


00:44:23.915 --> 00:44:25.974
How hot was the girl
on a scale of one to 10?


00:44:26.151 --> 00:44:28.085
- An 11.
- The hotness scale only goes 10.


00:44:28.253 --> 00:44:29.948
Yeah, this girl has love potential.


00:44:30.122 --> 00:44:32.420
- Ooh, love.
- Shut it.


00:44:33.792 --> 00:44:37.922
We are gonna do this for hours
until we get it right. Even if it takes hours.


00:44:38.897 --> 00:44:42.492
Now, sing like your life depends on it.
Because, sugar, it does.


00:44:43.568 --> 00:44:45.195
We're recording.


00:44:45.504 --> 00:44:47.335
<i>Plug in the mike</i>


00:44:47.506 --> 00:44:48.734
<i>Open the curtain</i>


00:44:49.341 --> 00:44:51.275
<i>Turn on the lights</i>


00:44:51.443 --> 00:44:53.172
<i>I'm through rehearsing</i>


00:44:53.345 --> 00:44:55.677
- Dang, she's good, man.
- Told you, man.


00:44:55.847 --> 00:44:57.075
Check this out, all right?


00:44:57.249 --> 00:45:00.844
Thirty-nine girls in the singing program
which means 85 percent...


00:45:01.019 --> 00:45:02.850
...have music during the sixth period.


00:45:03.021 --> 00:45:04.852
So your girl's in one of those rooms.


00:45:05.056 --> 00:45:07.081
<i>The feeling ignites</i>


00:45:07.259 --> 00:45:08.419
<i>I'm in control</i>


00:45:08.593 --> 00:45:10.561
Oh, cut. Cut.


00:45:10.729 --> 00:45:12.594
That was subpar at best.


00:45:12.764 --> 00:45:15.289
From the top, pretty please.


00:45:16.034 --> 00:45:19.333
<i>Amazing grace</i>


00:45:19.504 --> 00:45:21.062
It's cool, I got this.


00:45:21.239 --> 00:45:23.605
Ladies, all my single ladies.


00:45:23.775 --> 00:45:26.801
My boy Luke here has a special favor
to ask of you, all right?


00:45:26.978 --> 00:45:30.072
He needs vocals
for this big show coming up, so...


00:45:30.248 --> 00:45:31.806
- My name is...
- Luke Morgan.


00:45:32.250 --> 00:45:35.117
You will put me in the Showcase.
Oh, yes, you will.


00:45:35.654 --> 00:45:39.215
- Maybe I could ask you to sing first?
- I am so gonna rock your world.


00:45:39.491 --> 00:45:42.824
<i>I love the way you love me, Luke</i>


00:45:42.994 --> 00:45:45.588
<i>Inside my head every night</i>


00:45:45.764 --> 00:45:48.232
<i>You come and kiss me good night</i>


00:45:48.400 --> 00:45:51.494
<i>Whatever you see is what you get</i>


00:45:51.670 --> 00:45:54.195
Why don't you not suck
and do it again, okay?


00:45:55.941 --> 00:46:00.537
<i>I wanna be with you forever...</i>


00:46:00.712 --> 00:46:03.681
What is going on in here? Disgusting.


00:46:03.849 --> 00:46:06.682
You two boys are not in my class.
Stop. Wait.


00:46:12.724 --> 00:46:15.921
Stop. Wait. Stop.


00:46:35.046 --> 00:46:37.344
<i>I got nothing to lose</i>


00:46:37.515 --> 00:46:38.709
<i>I've been exposed</i>


00:46:38.884 --> 00:46:41.182
<i>I'm paying my dues</i>


00:46:41.353 --> 00:46:42.718
<i>Playing the role</i>


00:46:43.555 --> 00:46:45.682
- Oh, really?
- We are back where we started.


00:46:45.857 --> 00:46:46.983
This is not good.


00:46:48.560 --> 00:46:50.357
That's her. That's her voice.


00:46:50.528 --> 00:46:52.359
Don't think you can get away from me.


00:46:52.530 --> 00:46:54.930
- Step aside. Step aside.
- Please. Wait.


00:46:55.100 --> 00:46:58.536
Okay. But first, why don't you
just both audition for me.


00:46:58.703 --> 00:46:59.727
Listen...


00:46:59.905 --> 00:47:03.341
<i>Luke, you are the one for me, yes you are</i>


00:47:03.508 --> 00:47:05.169
<i>You just don't know it yet</i>


00:47:17.022 --> 00:47:21.015
<i>Make you believe in me</i>


00:47:21.192 --> 00:47:24.184
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:24.362 --> 00:47:27.991
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:28.166 --> 00:47:32.102
<i>That I can be
Anything, anything, anything</i>


00:47:32.270 --> 00:47:36.070
<i>I'll make you believe in me</i>


00:47:36.608 --> 00:47:39.509
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:39.678 --> 00:47:42.738
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:44.549 --> 00:47:46.483
It was you?


00:47:47.152 --> 00:47:50.246
- Oh, sorry to interrupt.
- Oh, no, honey. Interrupt away.


00:47:51.189 --> 00:47:55.023
I didn't think I'd see you. It was killing me.
Because I felt like we connected.


00:47:56.661 --> 00:47:59.687
Excuse me.
Uh, how exactly did you two connect?


00:47:59.864 --> 00:48:02.628
Yeah, how did we? I mean, we did.


00:48:02.801 --> 00:48:04.928
- Through...
- With your lyrics. They just...


00:48:05.570 --> 00:48:08.300
- I can't get them out of my head.
- My lyrics. Yeah.


00:48:08.573 --> 00:48:10.336
Well, how wonderful.


00:48:10.508 --> 00:48:13.875
But, uh, Bev has to prepare
for her Showcase audition.


00:48:14.045 --> 00:48:16.309
Oh, no. She doesn't need to audition.
You're in.


00:48:17.816 --> 00:48:19.613
Do you wanna grab a bite later?


00:48:19.784 --> 00:48:20.876
- Yeah.
Wait.


00:48:21.820 --> 00:48:23.287
You have a date with detention.


00:48:23.455 --> 00:48:24.922
Actually, he has a date with me.


00:48:25.090 --> 00:48:26.819
Dear me, did I not fire you?


00:48:26.992 --> 00:48:29.688
- I have tenure.
- One call and you're wearing a paper hat...


00:48:29.861 --> 00:48:32.989
...that says "Welcome to McDonald's.
How may I take your order?"


00:48:33.164 --> 00:48:34.654
- Five calls.
- Two calls and text.


00:48:34.833 --> 00:48:36.733
Two calls, a text, several long e-mails.


00:48:36.901 --> 00:48:39.699
One text and a Tweet.
- One text and a re-Tweet.


00:48:39.871 --> 00:48:42.237
Oh, for God's sakes,
go lick a chalkboard.


00:48:42.407 --> 00:48:43.874
Fine.


00:48:44.676 --> 00:48:46.200
I hate you.


00:48:49.848 --> 00:48:53.978
Okay. Um, I'd love to write a song with you.
Let's talk about it tonight?


00:48:54.252 --> 00:48:56.186
- I'd love to.
- Okay, you're on.


00:49:02.761 --> 00:49:04.388
I've always wanted to write a song.


00:49:04.562 --> 00:49:07.759
Maybe I'll write about my skin.
They say love tightens your pores.


00:49:07.932 --> 00:49:09.399
What rhymes with pores?


00:49:09.567 --> 00:49:12.365
Chores. Bores. Sores.


